    "etymology": {
     "text": "The article הַ־ + the pronoun הוּא “he” (הִיא “she”, הֵם / הֵן “they”): literally “the he”. Wiktionary lists הַהוּא as a determiner “that” and הַהִיא as its feminine.",
     "src": "Wiktionary (kaikki.org)"
    },
    "funFacts": [
     "Arabic also uses a separate “that” (ذٰلِكَ, تِلْكَ) but puts it before the noun: ذٰلِكَ الْبَيْتُ “that house” — Hebrew says “the house the-he”."
    ],
    "pitfalls": [
     "It comes after the noun, and the noun needs the article too: הַבַּיִת הַהוּא (not *בַּיִת הַהוּא, not *הַהוּא בַּיִת).",
